WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.095
Anthropic proved VP

00:00:01.907 --> 00:00:03.144
is not VNP

00:00:03.678 --> 00:00:04.326
You know the

00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:05.600
determinant from linear

00:00:05.423 --> 00:00:06.484
algebra class

00:00:06.623 --> 00:00:08.061
Using only addition

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:09.135
and multiplication

00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:10.066
it can still

00:00:09.878 --> 00:00:10.903
be computed in

00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:11.906
polynomial time

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.085
for example with

00:00:12.897 --> 00:00:14.335
Gaussian elimination

00:00:14.878 --> 00:00:15.868
The permanent is

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.741
like a determinant

00:00:16.553 --> 00:00:18.144
without any subtraction

00:00:18.215 --> 00:00:19.135
and no known

00:00:18.946 --> 00:00:19.995
method computes it

00:00:19.807 --> 00:00:21.175
in polynomial time

00:00:21.314 --> 00:00:22.210
For a matrix

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:22.905
of zeros and

00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:23.353
ones

00:00:23.413 --> 00:00:24.568
it is NP-hard

00:00:25.094 --> 00:00:26.662
Anthropic's proof says

00:00:26.474 --> 00:00:27.900
no polynomial-size

00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:28.879
arithmetic circuit

00:00:28.703 --> 00:00:29.669
can compute it

00:00:29.808 --> 00:00:30.704
So for P

00:00:30.516 --> 00:00:31.470
to equal NP

00:00:31.518 --> 00:00:32.319
some trick with

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.404
AND OR and

00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:34.077
NOT would have

00:00:33.888 --> 00:00:34.973
to beat addition

00:00:34.785 --> 00:00:36.199
and multiplication

00:00:36.726 --> 00:00:37.740
Full story on

00:00:37.551 --> 00:00:38.447
the dashboard
